{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q422504","formula":"C₉H₁₃N₃O₄","hill":"C9H13N3O4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":13.0,"N":3.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Deoxycytidine","ru":"Дезоксицитидин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Deoxycytidine is a deoxyribonucleoside, a component of deoxyribonucleic acid. It is similar to the ribonucleoside cytidine, but with one hydroxyl group removed from the C2' position. Deoxycytidine can be phosphorylated at C5' of the deoxyribose by deoxycytidine kinase, converting it to deoxycytidine monophosphate (dCMP), a DNA precursor.","ru":"Дезоксицитидин — нуклеозид, образующийся при соединении цитозина с дезоксирибозой β-N1-гликозидной связью. Дезоксицитидин является компонентом ДНК. В случае, если цитозин присоединен к рибозе, нуклеозид называется цитидином. Был одобрен в 2025 г."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":13711,"mass":227.22,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1[C@@H]([C@H](O[C@H]1N2C=CC(=NC2=O)N)CO)O","inchikey":"CKTSBUTUHBMZGZ-SHYZEUOFSA-N","iupac":"4-amino-1-[(2R,4S,5R)-4-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]pyrimidin-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"13711","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.474,"y":-0.221,"z":-0.978,"el":"O"},{"x":3.469,"y":1.865,"z":0.042,"el":"O"},{"x":2.508,"y":-2.779,"z":-0.489,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.597,"y":2.43,"z":-0.439,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.648,"y":0.344,"z":-0.172,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.029,"y":0.71,"z":-0.061,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.49,"y":-1.056,"z":0.328,"el":"N"},{"x":2.821,"y":0.777,"z":0.698,"el":"C"},{"x":1.379,"y":1.136,"z":0.976,"el":"C"},{"x":2.705,"y":-0.406,"z":-0.253,"el":"C"},{"x":0.699,"y":0.805,"z":-0.342,"el":"C"},{"x":2.625,"y":-1.743,"z":0.473,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.864,"y":-1.004,"z":0.061,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.755,"y":1.226,"z":-0.235,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.08,"y":-1.519,"z":0.232,"el":"C"},{"x":